f charge usually  playing any music or five hours talking  on the phone however if you do keep them  in the case they provide an additional  seven hours of charge which gives you a  total of about 13 hours maximum runtime  a second feature that I actually had no  idea about is the fact that they're  actually water resistant they have an IP  x2 rating which again I had to go up in  Google and find out what that actually  means and the definition by px2  is the fact that they're water-resistant  for anything hitting them at  fifteen degree angle now I don't know  how useful that is to you guys or how  useful that is going be to me but I'm  pretty much treating these headphones as  not really water-resistant  you shouldn't go swimming with them you  shouldn't go running in the rain with  them they're probably good enough to  withstand the gym sweat and you're gonna  get of everyday use I personally didn't  do a lot of research before I purchased  the Samsung Galaxy buds I didn't even  look at any youtube reviews so I wasn't  really too informed of what the specs  and features were when I got mine  originally I thought yes they have a  wireless charging what a great feature  and then I thought I wonder if it  charges my Samsung against a well  unfortunately if you've already looked  at a bunch reviews you know it doesn't  charge with anything but the Samsung S  10 which is really unfortunate because I  think wireless charging is basically  just a software update that samsa can do  it any time but hey I guess they really  got to keep their flagship models in  check and make sure you guys upgrade to  latest and greatest and make sure I  eventually upgrade to the S 10 as well  so when you look at the actual Samsung  bud earpieces you're gonna notice two  little gold specks on the inside and one  little black censor the black sensor  actually lets the earbuds know when  they're in your ear and when you place  them in they're going to make a little  tone and they also know when you pull  them out of your ear so they can go to  sleep and save battery straight away I  guess the main thing with any wireless  headphone and any headphone in general  is how good is the sound quality now I'm  gonna be a hundred percent honest with  you guys and it is good but it isn't  fantastic honestly the fact that these  little headphones do produce a sound  they do is amazing but they are missing  a little bit of bass I'm used to putting  on headphones like the Beats Studio  threes which have a ton of bass but  again they're huge over the ear  headphones which obviously can produce  that quality of sound these little guys  I've used for two weeks in the gym every  single day and not a single time have  they fallen out of my ears have they  been a problem they were a little bit  uncomfortable at the start but I think  that was just really a getting used to  it period and now they're completely  fine they sit in my ears completely  perfectly they never fall out and  they've lasted two weeks on a single  charge so that alone is incredible I  haven't had to go and plug them into the  charger  just popping my gym bag forgotten about  them and then when I'm done my workout  back into the charging case they go and  they charge ready for the next day  something that has annoyed me is the  fact that the headphones are adjusted by  tapping which I guess most headphones  are nowadays but the fact that these  headphones are so light and sit in your  ear  they almost kind of feel hollow when you  tap on them and the reverberation just  go straight into year so I actually have  to mentally think about it when I go to  tap and make sure that tap very lightly  so that ricochet doesn't go straight  into my head especially at like 5a in  the morning when you really don't want  to be hearing any extra noise continuing  here with the sound aspect of the  headphones the call quality on these  things is not amazing now I did watch a  video that the day that Samsung released  